## 7. Lockout/Tagout Devices

### 7.1 Authorized Devices

| Device Type | Description | Color Code |
|-------------|-------------|------------|
| **Personal Padlock** | Keyed-different lock issued to individual authorized employees; one key only | Red — Maintenance; Blue — Electrical; Orange — Contractor |
| **Department Lock** | Keyed-alike locks for department/shift lockouts | Yellow |
| **Group Lockbox** | Lockable box to hold isolation device keys during group lockout | Silver/Gray |
| **Lockout Hasps** | Multi-hole hasps for applying multiple locks to single isolation point | Red |
| **Danger Tags** | "DANGER — DO NOT OPERATE" tags with employee name, date, reason | Red/White/Black |
| **Valve Lockouts** | Ball valve, gate valve, and butterfly valve lockout devices | Red |
| **Circuit Breaker Lockouts** | Devices to lock circuit breakers in OFF position | Red |
| **Plug Lockouts** | Devices to secure electrical plugs | Red |
| **Pneumatic Lockouts** | Quick-disconnect lockout devices | Red |

### 7.2 Lock Assignment

- Each authorized employee is issued a personal lock with one unique key
- Locks are numbered and assigned in the LOTO lock register maintained by EHS
- Lost locks must be reported immediately to EHS Manager
- Duplicate keys are secured in EHS office safe and accessed only per Section 13 (Lock Removal Procedure)
- Locks remain the property of MMC and must be returned upon termination or role change

### 7.3 Tag Requirements

All lockout devices must be accompanied by a tag that includes:
- "DANGER — DO NOT OPERATE" header
- Employee name (printed)
- Employee signature
- Date and time applied
- Department
- Reason for lockout
- Expected duration (if known)

