## 8. Lockout/Tagout Procedure — Standard

### 8.1 Preparation (Before Lockout)

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Identify the equipment to be locked out | Authorized Employee |
| 2 | Locate the equipment-specific LOTO procedure (posted at equipment or in LOTO binder) | Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Identify all energy sources, isolation points, and stored energy | Authorized Employee |
| 4 | Notify affected employees and Supervisor that lockout will occur | Authorized Employee |
| 5 | Gather required lockout devices, tags, and tools | Authorized Employee |
| 6 | Review any special hazards or conditions | Authorized Employee |

### 8.2 Shutdown Sequence

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Notify machine operator that equipment will be shut down | Authorized Employee |
| 2 | If equipment is operating, shut down using normal stopping procedure | Operator or Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Verify all moving parts have come to complete stop | Authorized Employee |
| 4 | Ensure all personnel are clear of hazard zones | Authorized Employee |

### 8.3 Isolation and Lockout

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Operate energy isolating devices to isolate equipment from energy sources | Authorized Employee |
| 2 | Isolate in the following order: Electrical → Pneumatic → Hydraulic → Other | Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Apply personal lock to each energy isolating device | Authorized Employee |
| 4 | Attach completed "DANGER — DO NOT OPERATE" tag to each lock | Authorized Employee |
| 5 | Release, restrain, or dissipate all stored/residual energy | Authorized Employee |
| 6 | Block or support elevated components that could fall | Authorized Employee |

### 8.4 Stored Energy Dissipation

| Energy Type | Dissipation Method | Verification |
|-------------|-------------------|--------------|
| Electrical | Discharge capacitors; test with voltage meter | Zero voltage reading |
| Pneumatic | Bleed air from lines; open drain valves | Zero pressure on gauge; physical bleed confirmation |
| Hydraulic | Relieve pressure; cycle controls; bleed valves | Zero pressure on gauge |
| Mechanical | Release springs; block flywheels; relieve tension | Physical restraint in place |
| Thermal | Allow cool-down time per procedure | Temperature measurement below threshold |
| Chemical | Drain lines; purge with inert gas if required | Empty/purged confirmation |
| Gravity | Lower to ground or block/crib in place | Physical blocking verified |

### 8.5 Verification of Zero Energy State

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Verify all isolation devices are locked and tagged | Authorized Employee |
| 2 | Verify all stored energy has been dissipated or restrained | Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Ensure all personnel are clear of equipment | Authorized Employee |
| 4 | Attempt to start equipment using normal operating controls | Authorized Employee |
| 5 | Verify equipment does not start or energize | Authorized Employee |
| 6 | Return operating controls to OFF/NEUTRAL position | Authorized Employee |
| 7 | Test for absence of voltage (electrical) using calibrated meter | Authorized Employee (Qualified) |
| 8 | Document verification on LOTO permit (if required) | Authorized Employee |

**CRITICAL:** If equipment starts or energy is detected, STOP. Do not proceed. Re-evaluate isolation points and repeat lockout procedure.

### 8.6 Performing the Work

- Work only on equipment that has been verified at zero energy state
- Do not remove or bypass any lockout device during work
- If additional energy isolation is discovered during work, stop and apply additional lockout
- If work scope changes, re-evaluate hazards and update lockout as needed

### 8.7 Restoring Equipment to Service

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Verify work is complete and equipment is ready for operation | Authorized Employee |
| 2 | Remove all tools, materials, and debris from equipment | Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Replace all guards, covers, and safety devices | Authorized Employee |
| 4 | Verify all personnel are clear of equipment and hazard zones | Authorized Employee |
| 5 | Notify affected employees that lockout is being removed | Authorized Employee |
| 6 | Remove personal tag | Authorized Employee |
| 7 | Remove personal lock from energy isolating device | Authorized Employee (lock owner only) |
| 8 | Re-energize equipment in reverse order of isolation | Authorized Employee |
| 9 | Verify proper operation and notify Supervisor/Operator | Authorized Employee |
| 10 | Return equipment to production status | Line Supervisor |

