## 10. Group Lockout Procedure

Group lockout is required when:
- Two or more authorized employees work on the same equipment
- Work extends across shifts
- Multiple crafts or contractors are involved

### 10.1 Group Lockout Procedure

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Designate a primary authorized employee to coordinate the group lockout | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 2 | Primary authorized employee performs equipment shutdown and isolation per standard procedure | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Primary authorized employee applies lock and tag to each isolation point | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 4 | Primary authorized employee places isolation point keys in group lockbox | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 5 | Primary authorized employee applies personal lock to group lockbox | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 6 | Each additional authorized employee applies personal lock to group lockbox | Each Authorized Employee |
| 7 | Verification of zero energy state performed | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 8 | Work proceeds with all locks in place | All Authorized Employees |
| 9 | Upon work completion, each employee removes their personal lock from lockbox | Each Authorized Employee |
| 10 | Primary authorized employee removes their lock from lockbox last | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 11 | Primary authorized employee retrieves keys and removes locks from isolation points | Primary Authorized Employee |
| 12 | Equipment restored to service per standard procedure | Primary Authorized Employee |

### 10.2 Shift Transfer During Group Lockout

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Outgoing primary authorized employee briefs incoming primary | Both Primary Employees |
| 2 | Incoming primary authorized employee applies personal lock to lockbox | Incoming Primary Employee |
| 3 | Outgoing employees remove personal locks from lockbox | Outgoing Employees |
| 4 | Outgoing primary removes lock from lockbox last (after incoming primary's lock is applied) | Outgoing Primary Employee |
| 5 | Incoming shift employees apply personal locks to lockbox | Incoming Employees |
| 6 | Continuity of lockout documented on LOTO permit | Both Primary Employees |

**CRITICAL:** At no time shall the group lockbox be without at least one lock during an active group lockout.

