## 11. Contractor Lockout Requirements

### 11.1 Pre-Work Requirements

| Requirement | Responsibility |
|-------------|----------------|
| Review contractor's LOTO program for equivalency | EHS Manager |
| Conduct contractor safety orientation including LOTO | EHS / Maintenance Supervisor |
| Identify equipment and energy sources in scope of work | Maintenance Supervisor + Contractor |
| Provide equipment-specific LOTO procedures | Maintenance Supervisor |
| Issue contractor lockout devices (orange locks) or verify contractor devices meet MMC standards | Maintenance Supervisor |

### 11.2 Coordination Procedure

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | MMC authorized employee performs initial isolation and lockout | MMC Authorized Employee |
| 2 | MMC authorized employee verifies zero energy state | MMC Authorized Employee |
| 3 | Contractor authorized employee(s) apply personal locks to group lockbox or isolation points | Contractor |
| 4 | Work proceeds with all locks in place | Contractor |
| 5 | Contractor removes personal locks upon work completion | Contractor |
| 6 | MMC authorized employee verifies contractor locks removed | MMC Authorized Employee |
| 7 | MMC authorized employee performs verification and restores equipment | MMC Authorized Employee |

### 11.3 Contractor Isolation

If a contractor provides their own lockout:
- Contractor LOTO program must be reviewed and approved by EHS Manager
- Contractor must demonstrate equivalent protection per OSHA 1910.147
- MMC Maintenance Supervisor must be informed before lockout is applied
- MMC personnel do not operate contractor-locked equipment under any circumstances

