## 12. Tagout-Only Procedure

Tagout-only is permitted only when:
- The energy isolating device is not capable of being locked out, AND
- Full employee protection is demonstrated, AND
- EHS Manager has approved tagout-only in writing

### 12.1 Additional Safeguards for Tagout-Only

When tagout-only is used, the following additional measures are required:

| Additional Safeguard | Description |
|---------------------|-------------|
| Tag placement | Tag attached directly to energy isolating device |
| Warning communication | All affected employees verbally warned |
| Continuous monitoring | Additional employee stationed at tagout point (if feasible) |
| Enhanced verification | Additional testing and verification steps |
| Documentation | Written authorization from EHS Manager for each occurrence |
| Temporary measures | Physical barriers, additional warnings, or equipment removal |

### 12.2 Tag Removal Warning

**WARNING:** Tags are warning devices only and do not provide physical restraint. Tags must never be ignored, bypassed, or removed except by the employee who applied them.

---

## 13. Lock Removal Procedure (Absent Employee)

### 13.1 Conditions for Removal

A lock may be removed by someone other than the employee who applied it ONLY when:
- The employee who applied the lock is not available at the facility
- All reasonable efforts to contact the employee have been unsuccessful
- The procedure below is followed exactly

### 13.2 Removal Procedure

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Verify the employee who applied the lock is not on-site | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 2 | Attempt to contact the employee by phone (minimum 2 attempts, documented) | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 3 | If contact made, employee may verbally authorize removal after confirming work status | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 4 | If contact unsuccessful, notify EHS Manager | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 5 | EHS Manager authorizes lock removal in writing | EHS Manager |
| 6 | Maintenance Supervisor verifies equipment is safe for lock removal | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 7 | Obtain duplicate key from EHS office safe (two-person verification) | EHS Manager + Maintenance Supervisor |
| 8 | Remove lock and document removal with date, time, and circumstances | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 9 | Notify employee of lock removal before their next scheduled shift | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 10 | Employee acknowledges notification in writing upon return | Employee |
| 11 | Document entire process in LOTO incident log | EHS Manager |

### 13.3 Documentation Requirements

The following must be documented for any lock removal by non-owner:
- Name of employee whose lock was removed
- Name of employee(s) who removed the lock
- Date and time of removal
- Reason for removal
- Contact attempts and results
- Authorization from EHS Manager
- Notification to employee
- Employee acknowledgment

