## 14. Periodic Inspection (Annual Audit)

### 14.1 Inspection Requirements

- Annual inspection of LOTO procedures required per OSHA 1910.147(c)(6)
- Each equipment-specific procedure must be audited at least annually
- Inspection conducted by authorized employee other than those using the procedure

### 14.2 Inspection Procedure

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Schedule annual LOTO inspections by area | EHS Manager |
| 2 | Select authorized employee to perform inspection (not routine user of procedure) | EHS Manager |
| 3 | Inspector observes authorized employee applying lockout procedure | Inspector |
| 4 | Inspector verifies procedure followed correctly | Inspector |
| 5 | Inspector interviews authorized and affected employees on procedure understanding | Inspector |
| 6 | Inspector documents findings on LOTO Audit Form | Inspector |
| 7 | Deficiencies corrected and retraining conducted as needed | EHS Manager + Maintenance Supervisor |
| 8 | Audit documentation retained for minimum 3 years | EHS Manager |

### 14.3 Audit Checklist Elements

| Audit Element | Verify |
|---------------|--------|
| Procedure availability | Written procedure accessible at equipment |
| Energy source identification | All energy sources correctly identified |
| Isolation points | All isolation points correctly identified and labeled |
| Lockout device application | Lock and tag properly applied |
| Stored energy | Dissipation/restraint methods performed |
| Zero energy verification | Verification performed before work |
| Affected employee notification | Notification occurred |
| Equipment restoration | Guards replaced, verification performed |
| Employee knowledge | Understanding of procedure and responsibilities |

### 14.4 Corrective Actions

| Finding | Required Action |
|---------|-----------------|
| Procedure not followed | Retraining; document in personnel file |
| Procedure incomplete or incorrect | Revise procedure; retrain affected employees |
| Equipment isolation points not labeled | Label within 30 days |
| Lockout devices inadequate | Replace devices immediately |
| Repeat deficiency | Investigate root cause; implement corrective action |

