## 16. Documentation and Records

### 16.1 Required Documentation

| Document | Purpose | Retention |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| Equipment-specific LOTO procedures | Define lockout steps for each machine | Current + 3 years (superseded) |
| LOTO training records | Document employee training completion | Duration of employment + 3 years |
| Annual audit reports | Document periodic inspection results | 3 years |
| Lock register | Track lock assignments to employees | Current |
| LOTO permits (if used) | Document lockout for extended/group work | 1 year |
| Lock removal documentation | Record non-owner lock removals | 3 years |
| Incident reports | Document LOTO-related incidents | 5 years |

### 16.2 LOTO Permit

A LOTO Permit is required for:
- Group lockouts involving 3 or more authorized employees
- Lockouts extending across more than one shift
- Complex lockouts involving multiple systems
- Contractor lockouts

Permit contents:
- Equipment identification
- Work description
- All energy sources and isolation points
- Names of all authorized employees
- Date/time applied and expected completion
- Verification signatures
- Shift transfer documentation (if applicable)
- Completion sign-off

